/T (When evidence is presented in a courtroom, it is imperative that the integrity of the evidence has not been compromised. In criminal trials, the standard of proof for conviction is beyond a reasonable doubt, meaning that no rational or prudent  person would believe that the Defendant is innocent. It is the highest burden of proof required in law, as in civil cases the standard of proof is only preponderance of the evidence, meaning that the evidence points to the Defendant being guilty. These differences make sense because the penalties handed out in criminal cases )
