/T (a list of the most likely candidates from a massive database. The examiner then applies their expert judgment to confirm a match. Consequently, investigations move faster and the potential for error is significantly reduced.  Impression evidence, like shoe prints or tire tracks left in soil, provides valuable  clues about events at a crime scene. For years, the standard collection method  involved photography and making plaster casts. While effective, casts can be  fragile and may miss microscopic details. Today, a forensic investigator can use  portable 3D scanners to capture a perfect digital replica of the impression. )
/E (a list of the most likely candidates from a massive database. The examiner then applies their expert judgment to confirm a match. Consequently, investigations move faster and the potential for error is significantly reduced.  Impression evidence, like shoe prints or tire tracks left in soil, provides valuable  clues about events at a crime scene. For years, the standard collection method  involved photography and making plaster casts. While effective, casts can be  fragile and may miss microscopic details. Today, a forensic investigator can use  portable 3D scanners to capture a perfect digital replica of the impression. )
/Pg 24 0 R
