1921 0 obj
<<
/Title (Chain of Custody: The chronological, written record of the seizure, custody, control, transfer, analysis, and disposition of physical or electronic evidence  Evidence Integrity: The assurance that evidence, whether physical or digital,  remains authentic, unaltered, and untampered with from its collection to its  presentation in court  Preservation: The act of keeping something as it is, especially to prevent it from  being damaged, lost, or destroyed  Contamination: The process by which something becomes dirty, polluted, or  mixed with other substances in a way that makes it unreliable  Tampering: The act of touching or changing something without permission,  especially in a way that causes damage or makes it unreliable  Documentation: Written or recorded information that provides details or proof  about something  Admissibility: The quality of being accepted as evidence in a court of law  Authentication: The process of proving that something is real, true, or genuine  Procedure: A set of actions that is the official or accepted way of doing something  Transparency: The quality of being done in an open way so that people can easily see what actions have been taken  Accountability: The fact of being responsible for what you do and being able to  explain your actions  LIMS: Laboratory Information Management System  Sorensic Spoliation: the loss, destruction, or material alteration of an object or document that is evidence or potential evidence in a legal proceeding by one who has the responsibility for its preservation.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1919 0 R
>>
endobj
