1932 0 obj
<<
/Title (When evidence is presented in a courtroom, it is imperative that the integrity of the evidence has not been compromised. In criminal trials, the standard of proof for conviction is beyond a reasonable doubt, meaning that no rational or prudent  person would believe that the Defendant is innocent. It is the highest burden of proof required in law, as in civil cases the standard of proof is only preponderance of the evidence, meaning that the evidence points to the Defendant being guilty. These differences make sense because the penalties handed out in criminal cases)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1930 0 R
/Next 1936 0 R
>>
endobj
1933 0 obj
<<
/Title (So, what is the chain of custody? The definition of the chain of custody is the procedure, documentation, tracking, and protecting of evidence on its journey from a crime scene to the courtroom. This documentation process protects evidence  from contamination and tampering. It is also sometimes called the chain of evidence. If the chain of custody has been broken or tampered with, evidence can  be ruled as inadmissible, meaning it cannot be presented or believed to be  authentic in a court of law.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1930 0 R
/Prev 1936 0 R
>>
endobj
